target scan-hand
name: Your hand
object: hand
atomdex: element
references: ref-openstax-ap-elements
blurb: Your body is made of the same elements as everything else.
fun_fact: Oxygen, carbon, hydrogen and nitrogen are the four most abundant elements in the human body.

composition:
    {"symbol":"O"}
    {"symbol":"C"}
    {"symbol":"H"}
    {"symbol":"N"}

target scan-hair
name: A strand of hair
object: hair
references: ref-openstax-ap-hair
references: ref-openstax-ap-organic
blurb: Hair is a filament of keratin, a protein.

fun_fact:
    Every protein contains nitrogen, and many contain sulfur, together with carbon, hydrogen and oxygen. Keratin is a protein.

composition:
    {"symbol":"C"}
    {"symbol":"O"}
    {"symbol":"N","note":"in every protein"}
    {"symbol":"H"}
    {"symbol":"S","note":"found in many proteins"}

target scan-red-blood-cell
name: A red blood cell
object: rbc
references: ref-openstax-ap-erythrocytes
references: ref-openstax-ap-organic
blurb: A cell that carries oxygen around your body.
fun_fact: Hemoglobin, the molecule that carries oxygen in your blood, is made of proteins and iron.

